(4465532, 639732, 43156, '<td valign="top">Very impressive image, Lev. I like the candid feel, excellent B&amp;W conversion and tonal range.</td>', 'Very impressive image, Lev. I like the candid feel, excellent B&W conversion and tonal range.', '2008-02-06 17:15:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(4465684, 639432, 26255, '<td valign="top">It''s actually a very nice entry.  I like the sepia tones a lot and you managed to capture a lot of depth and detail in this image.  I love the subject and it certainly fits the challenge.  My only nitpick is the tightness of the crop on the bottom but that''s a minimal detail.  Good job!</td>', 'It''s actually a very nice entry.  I like the sepia tones a lot and you managed to capture a lot of depth and detail in this image.  I love the subject and it certainly fits the challenge.  My only nitpick is the tightness of the crop on the bottom but that''s a minimal detail.  Good job!', '2008-02-06 18:07:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4465706, 639737, 5885, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Quasimojo:</b></div><hr/><i> This is a fabulous shot but I really don''t want to sound like a DNMC hater but this really does feel like a shoehorn.  Maybe I don''t spend enough time in the kitchen but doesn''t everyone still use a wire whisk to beat eggs?!  It just doesn''t feel like ''old ways'' enough to me.  It''s a great image and it''s hard to mark you down for it, but I have to do a -1 out of respect to all the others that seem better interpreted imho  Brilliant shot in every other respect. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Irene, I think the image is awesome and congrats on the ribbon... but I too at first felt that it was a bit of a stretch. I couldn''t, however, force myself to vote it down low, because it is such a wonderful image.<br/> <br/>In retrospect, just because something is STILL done a certain way, does not make it not an old way.</td>', 'Originally posted by Quasimojo: This is a fabulous shot but I really don''t want to sound like a DNMC hater but this really does feel like a shoehorn.  Maybe I don''t spend enough time in the kitchen but doesn''t everyone still use a wire whisk to beat eggs?!  It just doesn''t feel like ''old ways'' enough to me.  It''s a great image and it''s hard to mark you down for it, but I have to do a -1 out of respect to all the others that seem better interpreted imho  Brilliant shot in every other respect.   Irene, I think the image is awesome and congrats on the ribbon... but I too at first felt that it was a bit of a stretch. I couldn''t, however, force myself to vote it down low, because it is such a wonderful image. In retrospect, just because something is STILL done a certain way, does not make it not an old way.', '2008-02-06 18:13:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(4465717, 640064, 86334, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the many comments.<br/> <br/>This image isn''t a great fit for ''old ways''. Building a snowman with my toddler kinda reminded me of my childhood, but it was still marginally appropriate at best.<br/> <br/>I liked the image. And it was what I was after when I set up the shot. The flash and framing (little or no cropping) created a bold image. So I decided to enter it even though it wasn''t a great fit for the challenge.<br/> <br/>Here in the Pacific Northwest it is not uncommon to have snowfall and a quick thaw. The lack of snow on my front yard was also a result of having used up much of it from the building of the snowman.<br/></td>', 'Thanks for the many comments. This image isn''t a great fit for ''old ways''. Building a snowman with my toddler kinda reminded me of my childhood, but it was still marginally appropriate at best. I liked the image. And it was what I was after when I set up the shot. The flash and framing (little or no cropping) created a bold image. So I decided to enter it even though it wasn''t a great fit for the challenge. Here in the Pacific Northwest it is not uncommon to have snowfall and a quick thaw. The lack of snow on my front yard was also a result of having used up much of it from the building of the snowman.', '2008-02-06 18:16:51.000000', NULL, 0),
