(4469344, 639351, 89341, '<td valign="top">Not bad for my first entry and using my point and shoot as I didn''t have my SLR lens :)<br/> <br/>The guy in blue wasn''t a dummy, he was actually operating the machine, I''d have liked to have used a slower shutter speed but he was jumping all over the place operating the machine!!<br/> <br/>A little surprised by the 1''s and 2''s though!<br/> <br/>Thanks for the pointer on colour saturation, have now just learnt how to use that function in PS :)</td>', 'Not bad for my first entry and using my point and shoot as I didn''t have my SLR lens :) The guy in blue wasn''t a dummy, he was actually operating the machine, I''d have liked to have used a slower shutter speed but he was jumping all over the place operating the machine!! A little surprised by the 1''s and 2''s though! Thanks for the pointer on colour saturation, have now just learnt how to use that function in PS :)', '2008-02-07 20:24:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470488, 638658, 30791, '<td valign="top">hey deb, first of all welcome back<br/>and congrats on 13th</td>', 'hey deb, first of all welcome backand congrats on 13th', '2008-02-08 07:31:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470984, 640039, 71459, '<td valign="top">Thanks Everyone! :)</td>', 'Thanks Everyone! :)', '2008-02-08 11:25:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471652, 639737, 90066, '<td valign="top">Wow...I really like this picture. You caught the egg yolk at what seems the perfect time.</td>', 'Wow...I really like this picture. You caught the egg yolk at what seems the perfect time.', '2008-02-08 17:42:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472032, 640037, 67697, '<td valign="top">Oh it''s good to see Gracie still moving around!  Great perspective.  And i love how she has that look on her face that says "and you expect this old body to climb those stairs?"  I also like how she''s been framed by the stairs and rails.</td>', 'Oh it''s good to see Gracie still moving around!  Great perspective.  And i love how she has that look on her face that says "and you expect this old body to climb those stairs?"  I also like how she''s been framed by the stairs and rails.', '2008-02-08 21:49:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472465, 639934, 87278, '<td valign="top">Congrats! Nice and quaint!</td>', 'Congrats! Nice and quaint!', '2008-02-09 03:48:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473041, 638771, 76335, '<td valign="top">I love the tones. Some of the greens and browns you coaxed out of the image are almost the color of... well, we don''t have to go there. <br/> <br/>Maybe it was by design, but the sky in the upper right is a bit noisy. Of course, I''m not sure how you could have fixed that (at least not in Basic editing) without losing some of the texture that really makes this image. <br/> <br/>5.2? I gave this a six and think it should have scored closer to that. Nice job!</td>', 'I love the tones. Some of the greens and browns you coaxed out of the image are almost the color of... well, we don''t have to go there.  Maybe it was by design, but the sky in the upper right is a bit noisy. Of course, I''m not sure how you could have fixed that (at least not in Basic editing) without losing some of the texture that really makes this image.  5.2? I gave this a six and think it should have scored closer to that. Nice job!', '2008-02-09 13:51:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473115, 639737, 69368, '<td valign="top">what an excellent work, Irene! Can''t believe you got 1, 2 and 3 for this fantastic shot!<br/>Big congrats on this deserved ribbon!</td>', 'what an excellent work, Irene! Can''t believe you got 1, 2 and 3 for this fantastic shot!Big congrats on this deserved ribbon!', '2008-02-09 14:49:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473168, 638400, 89452, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments and votes. Will have to work on more original ideas for future challenges.  Couldn''t believe how many camera shots were in the competition.</td>', 'Thanks for the comments and votes. Will have to work on more original ideas for future challenges.  Couldn''t believe how many camera shots were in the competition.', '2008-02-09 15:29:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4475465, 638898, 27133, '<td valign="top">Sorry for the DQ....but the vignette isn''t allowed in Basic.  I know...cause I got caught one before.</td>', 'Sorry for the DQ....but the vignette isn''t allowed in Basic.  I know...cause I got caught one before.', '2008-02-10 15:41:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4478182, 639934, 88523, '<td valign="top">Great shot! Reminds me of the years I spent in Washington Heights, NY.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-02-11 13:57:22.</i></td>', 'Great shot! Reminds me of the years I spent in Washington Heights, NY.', '2008-02-11 13:55:27.000000', '2008-02-11 13:57:22.000000', 0),
(4478596, 639737, 52992, '<td valign="top">wHAT an amazing shot Irene - I adore it.</td>', 'wHAT an amazing shot Irene - I adore it.', '2008-02-11 17:12:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(4478969, 639737, 43714, '<td valign="top">You sure have the touch, great shot!!!!!! Love it.</td>', 'You sure have the touch, great shot!!!!!! Love it.', '2008-02-11 20:34:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4480683, 640037, 66384, '<td valign="top">Oh, this makes me laugh. Even the dog thinks you''re nuts. As far as the image goes, I really like the lines of the steps, balusters and railing, and the floor boards and molding in the background.</td>', 'Oh, this makes me laugh. Even the dog thinks you''re nuts. As far as the image goes, I really like the lines of the steps, balusters and railing, and the floor boards and molding in the background.', '2008-02-12 14:51:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4481070, 638931, 75638, '<td valign="top">I agree with you, for sure, I despise partial desaturation, but it fits this picture perfectly. Great lighting, too! Is it a continuous source or a flash?</td>', 'I agree with you, for sure, I despise partial desaturation, but it fits this picture perfectly. Great lighting, too! Is it a continuous source or a flash?', '2008-02-12 18:06:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4509098, 639583, 69008, '<td valign="top">What can I say? Grate image? : ) <br/>Don''t feel bad. I have one in a current challenge that may show up right next to this in the "lowest rated" images pages. <br/>I see what you were shooting for here, but I think that I would have shot it from the other side, showing the potato, and with a little higher shutter speed. The voters don''t seem to vote happy on images that don''t have a strong subject that connects directly with the challenge description in their mind when they open the thumb.  At least you got this out of the way now, and can get back to going after other ribbons.</td>', 'What can I say? Grate image? : ) Don''t feel bad. I have one in a current challenge that may show up right next to this in the "lowest rated" images pages. I see what you were shooting for here, but I think that I would have shot it from the other side, showing the potato, and with a little higher shutter speed. The voters don''t seem to vote happy on images that don''t have a strong subject that connects directly with the challenge description in their mind when they open the thumb.  At least you got this out of the way now, and can get back to going after other ribbons.', '2008-02-23 01:20:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4517485, 640039, 56417, '<td valign="top">I love this.....it should have placed much higher IMO...; )</td>', 'I love this.....it should have placed much higher IMO...; )', '2008-02-26 07:14:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(4535341, 637203, 47169, '<td valign="top">I keep coming back to this shot, the amount of detail is amazing! To me every area of the image holds so much interest, it captivates me. Lovely color rendition and framing. Its even more amazing when you look at the camera settings! The D3 is quite a camera. You''ve caught me, now im off to look at the rest of your pictures!</td>', 'I keep coming back to this shot, the amount of detail is amazing! To me every area of the image holds so much interest, it captivates me. Lovely color rendition and framing. Its even more amazing when you look at the camera settings! The D3 is quite a camera. You''ve caught me, now im off to look at the rest of your pictures!', '2008-03-03 13:11:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4545999, 639252, 45475, '<td valign="top">This is a great comment. It is exactly the advice I would heed if I were you.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by citymars:</b></div><hr/><i> What a great old entrance, and I like the concept of the girl in front, but technically there are some problems: it''s not very sharp, the girl sort of disappears against the background, the upper left corner is too bright and draws the eye away from the subjects, a lot of empty space down front, plus you''ve got the phone wires.  Maybe shot at a later time of afternoon, with a tripod and a reflector or fill flash, would bring better results (though no recommendation for the wires, unless you can cut them down). ;-) </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'This is a great comment. It is exactly the advice I would heed if I were you. Originally posted by citymars: What a great old entrance, and I like the concept of the girl in front, but technically there are some problems: it''s not very sharp, the girl sort of disappears against the background, the upper left corner is too bright and draws the eye away from the subjects, a lot of empty space down front, plus you''ve got the phone wires.  Maybe shot at a later time of afternoon, with a tripod and a reflector or fill flash, would bring better results (though no recommendation for the wires, unless you can cut them down). ;-) ', '2008-03-07 15:22:54.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(4546103, 639239, 45475, '<td valign="top">Good subject for the challenge, nice light. The only faults I see are, the mess around the trike and the uninteresting angle of view. I think this could have been improved by simply taking this out to a clear area of snow, and getting down at level with the trike.</td>', 'Good subject for the challenge, nice light. The only faults I see are, the mess around the trike and the uninteresting angle of view. I think this could have been improved by simply taking this out to a clear area of snow, and getting down at level with the trike.', '2008-03-07 15:49:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4546142, 639651, 45475, '<td valign="top">Wow, now this is an improvement from your other shots. And a Pentax in it no less! Very clear and sharp. Good tones. My only nitpicks are that the angle is uninteresting and you have some distracting glare coming off the negatives.</td>', 'Wow, now this is an improvement from your other shots. And a Pentax in it no less! Very clear and sharp. Good tones. My only nitpicks are that the angle is uninteresting and you have some distracting glare coming off the negatives.', '2008-03-07 16:06:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(4561649, 639654, 57886, '<td valign="top">Interesting picture - I like the sepia tone, the light and shadows but think the picture would have been better if you could see more of the instrument. The title is good...<br/></td>', 'Interesting picture - I like the sepia tone, the light and shadows but think the picture would have been better if you could see more of the instrument. The title is good...', '2008-03-13 13:17:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4565280, 639782, 62787, '<td valign="top">Hey!<br/> <br/>Ok, you wanted me to have a look at this (finally got around to it - it''s been a busy time!)<br/> <br/>Some very interesting geometry in this shot - the interaction of horizontal and vertical lines all over the place looks pretty cool. The combination of the noise and the right chair blending into the horizontal stripes makes it look unreal, almost like an apparition rather than a real object. Old ways indeed. So I like the subject matter and the style.<br/> <br/>The composition doesn''t particularly work for me though. The centred window looks static and oddly cut off, and the directions of some of the diagonal beams make the picture feel tilted clockwise when viewed, even though it''s not. I think the picture would benefit greatly from losing that empty left bit (I tried cropping it, and it works a lot better for me).<br/> <br/>PP suggestions - since this is in basic, the options are rather limited. What I thought worked is sharpening this at about 45px, 30% usm to bring out the contrast more. I also liked the look of desating it very slightly (monochrome channel mixer layer, 100% red channel, 15% opacity), but that''s more a matter of taste, I think.<br/> <br/>Anyway, hope this helps.<br/> <br/>Jelena<br/> <br/></td>', 'Hey! Ok, you wanted me to have a look at this (finally got around to it - it''s been a busy time!) Some very interesting geometry in this shot - the interaction of horizontal and vertical lines all over the place looks pretty cool. The combination of the noise and the right chair blending into the horizontal stripes makes it look unreal, almost like an apparition rather than a real object. Old ways indeed. So I like the subject matter and the style. The composition doesn''t particularly work for me though. The centred window looks static and oddly cut off, and the directions of some of the diagonal beams make the picture feel tilted clockwise when viewed, even though it''s not. I think the picture would benefit greatly from losing that empty left bit (I tried cropping it, and it works a lot better for me). PP suggestions - since this is in basic, the options are rather limited. What I thought worked is sharpening this at about 45px, 30% usm to bring out the contrast more. I also liked the look of desating it very slightly (monochrome channel mixer layer, 100% red channel, 15% opacity), but that''s more a matter of taste, I think. Anyway, hope this helps. Jelena ', '2008-03-15 13:28:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4576811, 637909, 63267, '<td valign="top">This is a magnificant photo.  Everything about it is stunning.  I can''t imagine how you couldn''t have this hanging as a large print on your wall.  Brilliant!</td>', 'This is a magnificant photo.  Everything about it is stunning.  I can''t imagine how you couldn''t have this hanging as a large print on your wall.  Brilliant!', '2008-03-20 13:04:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4579707, 639934, 32767, '<td valign="top">Great shot! Geez, I rarely look at the front page these days so I missed this one. A belated congrats to a fellow New Yorker. I''m guessing you live up by Toms somewhere since a lot of your street shots are Upper West Siders? Probably a good place to shoot, still.</td>', 'Great shot! Geez, I rarely look at the front page these days so I missed this one. A belated congrats to a fellow New Yorker. I''m guessing you live up by Toms somewhere since a lot of your street shots are Upper West Siders? Probably a good place to shoot, still.', '2008-03-22 05:55:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4652263, 640036, 33769, '<td valign="top">holy cow thats a lot of expensive equipment!! :) wow- this is a really cool shot! :)</td>', 'holy cow thats a lot of expensive equipment!! :) wow- this is a really cool shot! :)', '2008-04-21 20:44:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4665374, 639015, 66635, '<td valign="top">This one is really nice.  Very sharp.  Good light.  Nice perspective.</td>', 'This one is really nice.  Very sharp.  Good light.  Nice perspective.', '2008-04-29 17:30:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4700903, 639651, 69008, '<td valign="top">I like this shot because it connects with my memory of the scent of fixer and developer, and nights spent poring over contact sheets looking for the "it factor" in the images to be printed.</td>', 'I like this shot because it connects with my memory of the scent of fixer and developer, and nights spent poring over contact sheets looking for the "it factor" in the images to be printed.', '2008-05-14 03:02:14.000000', NULL, 0),
